IMPORT prelude
-- EVERY-EACH-QUANTIFIER-SPEC §5.2 (RULED 2026-09-07 — R-Q7 for the anchor,
-- R-Q5 for the failure time; BUILT 2026-09-16): where an UNANCHORED WITHIN
-- inside a LEST counts from.
--
-- It counts from the FAILURE TIME, fixed by the layer the LEST attaches to
-- and then by the modal:
--
--   act layer, MUST / DO / MAY     the deadline that was missed;
--   act layer, SHANT               the violating event's own stamp;
--   state layer (ONCE … WITHIN)    the state's deadline.
--
-- Not from the event that revealed the miss, which is where it counted
-- until 2026-09-16. Under that rule a party who missed a deadline and then
-- stayed silent had no cure deadline until somebody else acted; under this
-- one silence changes nothing (§2).
--
-- There is ONE mechanism. A single obligation chooses its LEST's clock at
-- its own expiry (Machine.hs, Contract5: the deadline; Contract10: the
-- violating stamp), and a barrier member IS a single obligation, so the
-- barrier's LEST counts from the earliest-failing member's deadline with no
-- rule of its own. `WITHIN d` and `WITHIN d OF THE DEADLINE` under a LEST
-- therefore name one instant for every failure but a SHANT violation, and
-- §1, §3 and §6 pin the two spellings side by side. The breach's own date
-- is NOT moved: a breach is still dated at the event that revealed it, and
-- carries the deadline it missed (spec §3.4). Because a LEST counts from
-- the deadline, one event can be past several LEST layers at once; it is
-- offered to each in turn until it reaches a layer whose window is still
-- open (§9) — including a layer whose deadline is no later than the one
-- before it (§11) — and the clock a continuation is applied to is also
-- what THE ARMING names inside it (§10). The one chain that walk cannot
-- end, a continuation that reaches itself with its deadline already past,
-- is refused by name (§12).

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    Landlord HAS name IS A STRING
    Tenant   HAS name IS A STRING

DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    Sign    HAS signer IS AN Actor
    Refund  HAS who    IS AN Actor
    Smoke   HAS who    IS AN Actor
    Approve HAS who    IS AN Actor

theLandlord MEANS Landlord OF "Ms Ng"
alice       MEANS Tenant OF "Alice"
bob         MEANS Tenant OF "Bob"
carol       MEANS Tenant OF "Carol"
tenants     MEANS LIST alice, bob, carol
`tenants, reversed` MEANS LIST carol, bob, alice

-- Carol, LAST on the roll, has the EARLIEST deadline (5); Bob and Alice
-- have 14.
GIVEN t IS AN Actor
GIVETH A NUMBER
`days allowed to` t MEANS IF t EQUALS carol THEN 5 ELSE 14


§ `1. a single obligation: the spec's own probe`

-- Alice must sign by 10; if she does not, the landlord must refund within 5.
-- The miss comes to light at 14 (a WAIT). The refund's five days count from
-- 10, the deadline Alice missed, so the refund is due at 15: at 14 one day
-- remains; a refund at 15 is timely; a refund at 18 is late and the breach
-- reports 15. (Until 2026-09-16 the five days counted from 14, the refund
-- was due at 19, and the refund at 18 was FULFILLED.)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`sign or refund` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign alice WITHIN 10
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  (PARTY theLandlord MUST Refund theLandlord WITHIN 5)

#TRACE `sign or refund` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 14)

#TRACE `sign or refund` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 14)
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 15

#TRACE `sign or refund` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 14)
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 18

-- The same clock said out loud: `OF THE DEADLINE` names the instant the
-- unanchored form now counts from. Same residual, same breach.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`sign or refund, anchored` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign alice WITHIN 10
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  (PARTY theLandlord MUST Refund theLandlord WITHIN 5 OF THE DEADLINE)

#TRACE `sign or refund, anchored` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 14)

#TRACE `sign or refund, anchored` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 14)
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 18

-- The revealing event is still re-offered to the LEST, so a refund that is
-- itself the first thing after the deadline can discharge it: at 14 it is
-- timely (14 ≤ 15). At 18 the same refund reveals Alice's miss, is
-- re-offered, reveals the refund's own expiry too — the deadline anchor is
-- what makes that possible — and, the refund having no LEST of its own,
-- the walk ends there: the breach reports 15.
#TRACE `sign or refund` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 14

#TRACE `sign or refund` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 18


§ `2. silence does not postpone the cure period`

-- Nothing at all happens until 100. The refund fell due at 15 regardless,
-- and the WAIT that reveals Alice's miss reveals the landlord's too: the
-- breach reports 15. (Until 2026-09-16 the refund's clock started at 100
-- and the answer was a residual with five days on it.)
#TRACE `sign or refund` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 100)


§ `3. a barrier: the LEST counts from the earliest-failing member's deadline`

-- run-stack.l4 §1–3 pin this rule with `WITHIN 5 OF THE DEADLINE`; here the
-- WITHIN is unanchored and the numbers are the same. Alice signs at 1. Carol
-- misses 5 (revealed at 8), Bob misses 14 (revealed at 20). The LEST is
-- anchored at Carol's failure — her deadline, 5 — so the refund is due at
-- 10: at 10 FULFILLED, at 11 BREACHED reporting 10, on both rolls. Were the
-- clock the revealing event's (8) the refund would be due 13 and both
-- refunds timely.
GIVEN roll IS A LIST OF Actor
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`staggered` roll MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN roll
        MUST   Sign t
        WITHIN `days allowed to` t
        ONCE   ALL HAVE
        HENCE  FULFILLED
        LEST   (PARTY theLandlord MUST Refund theLandlord WITHIN 5)

#TRACE `staggered` tenants AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 8)
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 10
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)

#TRACE `staggered` tenants AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 8)
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 11
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)

#TRACE `staggered` `tenants, reversed` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 8)
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 11
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)

-- Both misses revealed by one WAIT UNTIL 20: the anchor is Carol's 5, not
-- Bob's 14 and not the 20 that revealed them, so the refund was due at 10
-- on both rolls. The revealing WAIT, re-offered to the LEST, already lies
-- past that: the breach reports 10, dated at the WAIT (20), and the refund
-- at 21 is never reached.
#TRACE `staggered` tenants AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 21

#TRACE `staggered` `tenants, reversed` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 21

-- The anchored twin, on the first trace: the same 10.
GIVEN roll IS A LIST OF Actor
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`staggered, anchored` roll MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN roll
        MUST   Sign t
        WITHIN `days allowed to` t
        ONCE   ALL HAVE
        HENCE  FULFILLED
        LEST   (PARTY theLandlord MUST Refund theLandlord WITHIN 5 OF THE DEADLINE)

#TRACE `staggered, anchored` tenants AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 8)
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 11
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)


§ `4. a fork: each member's LEST counts from that member's own deadline`

-- Under UPON EACH every member carries its own LEST. Bob and Carol never
-- sign. Carol's refund is due 5 + 5 = 10, Bob's 14 + 5 = 19: two refunds are
-- owed, and each member's reparation sees only what followed its own miss.
-- Refunds at 10 and 19 discharge both; a second refund at 20 instead is late
-- for Bob's, and the breach reports 19.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`each signs or refund` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN LIST bob, carol
        MUST   Sign t
        WITHIN `days allowed to` t
        UPON   EACH
        HENCE  FULFILLED
        LEST   (PARTY theLandlord MUST Refund theLandlord WITHIN 5)

#TRACE `each signs or refund` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 8)
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 10
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 19

#TRACE `each signs or refund` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 8)
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 10
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 20


§ `5. SHANT: the clock is the violation itself, and THE DEADLINE is something else`

-- A prohibition fails at the act, not at a deadline (R-Q5). Alice smokes at
-- 3; the landlord's five days to refund count from 3 and end at 8: a refund
-- at 8 is timely, at 9 the breach reports 8. This is the one failure where
-- the unanchored clock and `OF THE DEADLINE` part company: THE DEADLINE in a
-- SHANT's LEST is the window's end, 14, so the anchored twin is due at 19
-- and a refund at 9 is timely there.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`no smoking` MEANS
    PARTY alice SHANT Smoke alice WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  (PARTY theLandlord MUST Refund theLandlord WITHIN 5)

#TRACE `no smoking` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Smoke alice AT 3
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 8

#TRACE `no smoking` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Smoke alice AT 3
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 9

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`no smoking, anchored` MEANS
    PARTY alice SHANT Smoke alice WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  (PARTY theLandlord MUST Refund theLandlord WITHIN 5 OF THE DEADLINE)

#TRACE `no smoking, anchored` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Smoke alice AT 3
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 9


§ `6. the state layer: the LEST sees only what followed the state deadline`

-- Everyone signs, but the last signature lands after the ONCE line's
-- deadline of 10. The LEST is anchored at 10 and `THE DEADLINE` names it —
-- that was already so — and it is now handed the events after 10 only.
-- A refund at 1, before anyone had acted, no longer discharges it: the
-- refund is due at 15, and the WAIT at 20 reveals its expiry, reporting 15.
-- (Until 2026-09-16 this LEST was handed the whole stream from the arming
-- and the refund at 1 made it FULFILLED.)
GIVEN roll IS A LIST OF Actor
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`bounded` roll MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN roll
        MUST   Sign t
        WITHIN 14
        ONCE   ALL HAVE WITHIN 10
        HENCE  FULFILLED
        LEST   (PARTY theLandlord MUST Refund theLandlord WITHIN 5)

#TRACE `bounded` tenants AT 0 WITH
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 1
  PARTY carol DOES Sign carol AT 3
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 4
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 12
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)

-- A refund at 11 — after the state deadline, before Bob's late signature —
-- is in the stream the LEST sees, and discharges it. (The join's own
-- residual, what followed the LAST signature, would have missed it: that
-- stream starts after 12.)
#TRACE `bounded` tenants AT 0 WITH
  PARTY carol DOES Sign carol AT 3
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 4
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 11
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 12
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)

-- Boundary and breach: a refund at 15 is timely, at 16 the breach reports 15.
#TRACE `bounded` tenants AT 0 WITH
  PARTY carol DOES Sign carol AT 3
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 4
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 12
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 15

#TRACE `bounded` tenants AT 0 WITH
  PARTY carol DOES Sign carol AT 3
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 4
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 12
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 16

-- The anchored twin, on the refund-at-1 trace: the same 15.
GIVEN roll IS A LIST OF Actor
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`bounded, anchored` roll MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN roll
        MUST   Sign t
        WITHIN 14
        ONCE   ALL HAVE WITHIN 10
        HENCE  FULFILLED
        LEST   (PARTY theLandlord MUST Refund theLandlord WITHIN 5 OF THE DEADLINE)

#TRACE `bounded, anchored` tenants AT 0 WITH
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 1
  PARTY carol DOES Sign carol AT 3
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 4
  PARTY bob   DOES Sign bob   AT 12
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)


§ `7. MAY and DO: a lapse fails at the deadline, as a MUST does`

-- A permission not exercised by 5 routes to the LEST (README's default
-- matrix), and the LEST counts from 5: at 8 the refund has two days left;
-- at 10 it is timely; at 11 the breach reports 10.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`may approve or refund` MEANS
    PARTY alice MAY Approve alice WITHIN 5
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  (PARTY theLandlord MUST Refund theLandlord WITHIN 5)

#TRACE `may approve or refund` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 8)

#TRACE `may approve or refund` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 8)
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 10

#TRACE `may approve or refund` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 8)
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 11

-- DO is the bare form and behaves as MUST: at 14 one day remains.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`do sign or refund` MEANS
    PARTY alice DO Sign alice WITHIN 10
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  (PARTY theLandlord MUST Refund theLandlord WITHIN 5)

#TRACE `do sign or refund` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 14)


§ `8. a chain: the second chance runs from the first deadline`

-- The tutorial's late fee. Alice must sign by 7; missing that, she has
-- fourteen more days — from 7, so until 21, whatever day the miss came to
-- light. At 8 thirteen days remain; a signature at 21 is timely; at 22 the
-- inner LEST BREACH is the answer.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`sign, with a second chance` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign alice WITHIN 7
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  (PARTY alice MUST Sign alice WITHIN 14
           HENCE FULFILLED
           LEST BREACH BY alice BECAUSE "the second chance was missed too")

#TRACE `sign, with a second chance` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 8)

#TRACE `sign, with a second chance` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 8)
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 21

#TRACE `sign, with a second chance` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 8)
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 22


§ `9. a LEST that names itself still terminates`

-- Each incarnation counts from the previous one's missed deadline: the
-- windows are (0,3], (3,6], (6,9], … The WAIT at 100 reveals the expiry of
-- every incarnation whose deadline is below 100 — thirty-three of them —
-- and is re-offered to each in turn, because each one's deadline is later
-- than the last; it reaches the thirty-fourth, armed at 99 and due at 102,
-- which it does not expire, and that incarnation is the residual with two
-- days left. A signature at 101 after it falls in that same window and
-- fulfils it. Evaluation terminates because the deadlines an event walks
-- strictly increase and stop below its stamp. (Until the adversarial pass
-- of 2026-09-16 an event was re-offered AT MOST once and consumed on its
-- second expiry, so the WAIT reached only the third incarnation, which then
-- printed WITHIN 3 with its deadline 91 days in the past, and the signature
-- at 101 — timely for the incarnation live at 101 — was dropped.)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`sign, or try again` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign alice WITHIN 3
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  `sign, or try again`

#TRACE `sign, or try again` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 100)

#TRACE `sign, or try again` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 100)
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 101

-- Three layers, and ONE event past the first two: the signature at 100 is
-- offered to the first (due 3), the second (due 6) and the third (due 106),
-- which it performs in time. Whether somebody else's event came earlier
-- makes no difference to the verdict.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`third chance` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign alice WITHIN 3
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  (PARTY alice MUST Sign alice WITHIN 3
           HENCE FULFILLED
           LEST  (PARTY alice MUST Sign alice WITHIN 100
                  HENCE FULFILLED
                  LEST  BREACH BY alice BECAUSE "all three chances missed"))

#TRACE `third chance` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 100

#TRACE `third chance` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY bob DOES Approve bob AT 7
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 100

-- The same three layers with every window missed (due 3, 6, 9): one event
-- at 100, or two, is the same breach.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`three chances` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign alice WITHIN 3
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  (PARTY alice MUST Sign alice WITHIN 3
           HENCE FULFILLED
           LEST  (PARTY alice MUST Sign alice WITHIN 3
                  HENCE FULFILLED
                  LEST  BREACH BY alice BECAUSE "all three chances missed"))

#TRACE `three chances` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 100)

#TRACE `three chances` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 100)
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 101


§ `10. THE ARMING of a LEST continuation is the failure time`

-- A continuation is applied to the clock its LEST counts from, and that is
-- what THE ARMING names one level further down. Alice misses 10; the
-- landlord's refund counts from 10, and Bob's approval, anchored OF THE
-- ARMING of the refund obligation, is due at 10 + 3 = 13 — not at the WAIT
-- that revealed the miss (14) plus 3. The refund at 16 fires the HENCE; the
-- WAIT at 16 then reveals that Bob's window closed at 13.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`arming under lest` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign alice WITHIN 10
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  (PARTY theLandlord MUST Refund theLandlord WITHIN 20
           HENCE (PARTY bob MUST Approve bob WITHIN 3 OF THE ARMING))

#TRACE `arming under lest` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 14)
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 16
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 16)

-- Under HENCE nothing moved: the continuation is applied at the act, so
-- THE ARMING read two levels down under a HENCE is that act's stamp.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`arming under hence` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign alice WITHIN 10
    HENCE (PARTY theLandlord MUST Refund theLandlord WITHIN 20
           HENCE (PARTY bob MUST Approve bob WITHIN 3 OF THE ARMING))

#TRACE `arming under hence` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 4
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 6
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 8)


§ `11. a layer whose deadline does not advance is walked, not skipped`

-- Three layers: Alice must sign by 10; failing that, by 5 OF THE ARMING —
-- the enclosing obligation's arming, 0, so a window that had already
-- closed when the layer was entered; failing that, the landlord refunds
-- WITHIN 10 of that layer's deadline, 5, so by 15. A refund at 12 is the
-- first thing after 10: it reveals Alice's miss, is handed to the second
-- layer, reveals that miss too — at a deadline EARLIER than the one it had
-- just revealed — and is handed on again to the third, which it performs
-- in time. A WAIT at 11 before it changes nothing. At 20 the same refund
-- is late for the third layer, with or without the WAIT: the breach
-- reports 15. (Until round 2 of the adversarial pass of 2026-09-16 a copy
-- whose deadline had not advanced was consumed at the second layer, so
-- the refund at 12 alone left the third layer as an untouched residual
-- and the refund at 20 alone did the same, while the traces with the WAIT
-- gave FULFILLED and the breach — one instant, two verdicts.)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`stuck in the middle` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign alice WITHIN 10
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  (PARTY alice MUST Sign alice WITHIN 5 OF THE ARMING
           HENCE FULFILLED
           LEST  (PARTY theLandlord MUST Refund theLandlord WITHIN 10))

#TRACE `stuck in the middle` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 12

#TRACE `stuck in the middle` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 11)
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 12

#TRACE `stuck in the middle` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 20

#TRACE `stuck in the middle` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 11)
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 20

-- A `WITHIN 0` second chance — sign forthwith — is the same shape with the
-- deadline EQUAL to the one before it (10, 10, then 15): the refund at 12
-- reaches the third layer, with or without the WAIT; at 20 it is late.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`forthwith` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign alice WITHIN 10
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  (PARTY alice MUST Sign alice WITHIN 0
           HENCE FULFILLED
           LEST  (PARTY theLandlord MUST Refund theLandlord WITHIN 5))

#TRACE `forthwith` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 12

#TRACE `forthwith` AT 0 WITH
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 11)
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 12

#TRACE `forthwith` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 20


§ `12. a chain that cannot end is refused, by name`

-- A LEST that names itself with `WITHIN 0` counts every incarnation from
-- the deadline the last one missed, so every incarnation is due at 0 and
-- already past when it is entered: the event at 50 can never reach a layer
-- whose window is open. Walking such a chain forever is the only thing
-- the §11 rule cannot do, so after a thousand hand-offs in a row without
-- the deadline advancing the machine refuses the contract and says why.
-- (deontic-breach-semantics.l4 (f) pins the negative-WITHIN form.)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`forthwith, forever` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign alice WITHIN 0
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  `forthwith, forever`

#TRACE `forthwith, forever` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 50
